  "solution": {
    "text": "Octane number is defined as the percentage by volume of iso-octane present in the mixture of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mrow></math> and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mrow></math> which has the same antiknocking properties as the fuel under examination. <br/><br/>Given fuel (25% n-heptane +75% iso-octane) Hence, octane number = 75 (because iso octane is 75%)",
    "image": null
  },
